\f0\b\fs28 \cf2 \strokec2 Domain Functional Specifications\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa160\partightenfactor0

\fs24 \cf2 Program Parameters (Top-Level Architecture)\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0 \cf2 Defines structural training components including Primary Split Strategy (
\fs30 \cf3 \cb4 \strokec3 PPL
\fs24 \cf2 \cb1 \strokec2 , 
\fs30 \cf3 \cb4 \strokec3 Upper_Lower
\fs24 \cf2 \cb1 \strokec2 , 
\fs30 \cf3 \cb4 \strokec3 Full_Body
\fs24 \cf2 \cb1 \strokec2 ), Microcycle Frequency ($3$ to $6$ days per week), and Target Session Duration ($30$, $45$, $60$, $75+$ minutes). Modifying any Program Parameter forces a complete re-compilation of the active mesocycle schedule.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa160\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf2 Methodology Preferences\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0 \cf2 Controls engine heuristics within established program structures. Key variables include Movement Selection Bias (
\fs30 \cf3 \cb4 \strokec3 Stretch_Focused
\fs24 \cf2 \cb1 \strokec2 , 
\fs30 \cf3 \cb4 \strokec3 SFR_Optimized
\fs24 \cf2 \cb1 \strokec2 , 
\fs30 \cf3 \cb4 \strokec3 Compound_Heavy
\fs24 \cf2 \cb1 \strokec2 ), Proximity-to-Failure Policy (
\fs30 \cf3 \cb4 \strokec3 Target_RIR_Ramp
\fs24 \cf2 \cb1 \strokec2 , 
\fs30 \cf3 \cb4 \strokec3 Fixed_RIR
\fs24 \cf2 \cb1 \strokec2 ), Progression Schemes (
\fs30 \cf3 \cb4 \strokec3 Double_Progression
\fs24 \cf2 \cb1 \strokec2 , 
\fs30 \cf3 \cb4 \strokec3 Dynamic_Double_Progression
\fs24 \cf2 \cb1 \strokec2 ), and Volume Aggressiveness Multipliers ($0.8\\times$ to $1.2\\times$ baseline velocity).\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa160\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf2 Operational Constraints\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0 \cf2 Acts as a dynamic filter on the exercise database prior to movement pattern slotting. Includes Equipment Availability Bitmasks (
\fs30 \cf3 \cb4 \strokec3 Barbell
\fs24 \cf2 \cb1 \strokec2 , 
\fs30 \cf3 \cb4 \strokec3 Dumbbell
\fs24 \cf2 \cb1 \strokec2 , 
\fs30 \cf3 \cb4 \strokec3 Cable
\fs24 \cf2 \cb1 \strokec2 , 
\fs30 \cf3 \cb4 \strokec3 Plate_Loaded
\fs24 \cf2 \cb1 \strokec2 , 
\fs30 \cf3 \cb4 \strokec3 Bodyweight
\fs24 \cf2 \cb1 \strokec2 ) and Joint/Pain Constraints (
\fs30 \cf3 \cb4 \strokec3 Flexion_Intolerant_Lumbar
\fs24 \cf2 \cb1 \strokec2 , 
\fs30 \cf3 \cb4 \strokec3 Subacromial_Impingement
\fs24 \cf2 \cb1 \strokec2 , 
\fs30 \cf3 \cb4 \strokec3 Patellar_Tendinopathy
\fs24 \cf2 \cb1 \strokec2 ).\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa160\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf2 User Experience Prior\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0 \cf2 Replaces static experience scalars with an Individualized Historical Baseline ($V_\{base\}$) derived from user-reported training volume over the preceding eight weeks. This value initializes the starting microcycle volume budget.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa160\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf2 Educational & Scientific Library\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0 \cf2 Houses verified exercise physiology documentation. These assets configure zero engine code directly; instead, they provide structured context for LLM Coach interactions, enabling accurate, evidence-backed user feedback.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\fs28 \cf7 \cb8 \strokec7 USER SETTINGS INTERFACE\
  |\
  +---> Program Parameters        --> Triggers Full Mesocycle Re-Plan\
  +---> Methodology Preferences   --> Triggers Exercise Slotting Re-Plan\
  +---> Operational Constraints   --> Triggers Dynamic Exercise Filtering\
  +---> User Experience Prior     --> Seeds Microcycle Baseline (V_base)\
  +---> Educational Library       --> Injects Context into LLM Coach\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa160\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf2 \cb1 \strokec2 Preference Negotiation Workflow\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf2 When a user alters a methodology preference (e.g., switching selection bias from 
\fs30 \cf3 \cb4 \strokec3 Compound_Heavy
\fs24 \cf2 \cb1 \strokec2  to 
\fs30 \cf3 \cb4 \strokec3 Stretch_Focused
\fs24 \cf2 \cb1 \strokec2 ), the app executes a structured state update:\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls2\ilvl0\cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	1	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 The UI captures the selection and writes the change to the persistent 
\fs30 \cf3 \cb4 \strokec3 MemoryProfile
\fs24 \cf2 \cb1 \strokec2  struct.\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls2\ilvl0
\fs30 \cf3 \cb4 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	2	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec3 MemoryProfile
\fs24 \cf2 \cb1 \strokec2  emits an update event to 
\fs30 \cf3 \cb4 \strokec3 PlanKit
\fs24 \cf2 \cb1 \strokec2  and 
\fs30 \cf3 \cb4 \strokec3 PrescriptionEngine
\fs24 \cf2 \cb1 \strokec2 .\
\ls2\ilvl0
\fs30 \cf3 \cb4 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	3	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec3 PrescriptionEngine
\fs24 \cf2 \cb1 \strokec2  re-slotifies the active microcycle session array, selecting candidate exercises that emphasize long muscle length loading patterns.\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls2\ilvl0\cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	4	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 The engine passes the updated session plan to the LLM Coach alongside corresponding citations from the Educational Library (e.g., Maeo et al., 2023; Wolf et al., 2023).\
\ls2\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	5	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
