\f0\b\fs28 \cf2 \strokec2 Two-Exercise Session Validation Rules\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf2 A session containing only two exercise slots is classified as an engine 
\f0\b Defect
\f1\b0  unless one of the following validated system conditions is active:\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls3\ilvl0
\f0\b \cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	1	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Time Budget Limit
\f1\b0 : User active time budget is set to $30\\text\{ minutes\}$.\
\ls3\ilvl0
\f0\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	2	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Readiness Depressed
\f1\b0 : Morning Readiness (ARC) score falls below $0.40$, triggering an automated volume reduction to prevent excessive fatigue.\
\ls3\ilvl0
\f0\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	3	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Deload Phase
\f1\b0 : Active microcycle phase is flagged as 
\fs30 \cf3 \cb4 \strokec3 Deload
\fs24 \cf2 \cb1 \strokec2 , reducing targets to Maintenance Volume ($MV$, $\\sim 50\\%$ of baseline volume).\
\ls3\ilvl0
\f0\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	4	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Acute Joint Constraint
\f1\b0 : Active pain constraints exclude $\\ge 50\\%$ of candidate movement patterns for the targeted muscle groups.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa160\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs28 \cf2 \strokec2 Overlap and Synergy Set Accounting Logic\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf2 To track fatigue and volume accurately without double-counting set totals, Helm utilizes a dual-tier set credit system:\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls4\ilvl0
\f0\b \cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Direct Set Credit (1.0)
\f1\b0 : Granted to primary mover muscles in a movement pattern (e.g., Barbell Incline Bench Press grants 1.0 set credit to Pectoralis Major).\
\ls4\ilvl0
\f0\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Synergy Set Credit (0.5)
\f1\b0 : Granted to primary synergist muscles receiving substantial mechanical tension and proximity to failure (e.g., Barbell Incline Bench Press grants 0.5 set credit to Anterior Deltoid and Triceps Brachii).\
\ls4\ilvl0
\f0\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Stabilizer Credit (0.0)
\f1\b0 : Secondary postural stabilizers receive 0.0 set credit toward hypertrophic volume landmarks, but their mechanical contribution is logged for systemic fatigue calculations (e.g., Erector Spinae during Barbell Rows).\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\fs28 \cf7 \cb8 \strokec7 MOVEMENT INPUT: Barbell Incline Bench Press (3 Hard Sets Performed)\
  |\
  +---> Pectoralis Major (Primary Mover)  --> 1.0 Credit x 3 Sets = 3.0 Direct Sets Logged\
  +---> Anterior Deltoid (Synergist)      --> 0.5 Credit x 3 Sets = 1.5 Synergy Sets Logged\
  +---> Triceps Brachii (Synergist)       --> 0.5 Credit x 3 Sets = 1.5 Synergy Sets Logged\
  +---> Erector Spinae (Stabilizer)       --> 0.0 Credit x 3 Sets = 0.0 Hypertrophy Credit (Fatigue Only)\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa160\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf2 \cb1 \strokec2 Deterministic Session Composer Algorithm\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0 \cf7 \cb8 \strokec7 Algorithm: DeterministicSessionComposer\
Input:\
    TargetMuscles: Array of Muscle Enums for active day split\
    WeeklySetBudgets: Map<Muscle, Int> derived from PlanKit MEV->MRV models\
    RemainingSessionsInMicrocycle: Map<Muscle, Int>\
    TimeBudgetMinutes: Int\
    EquipmentMask: Bitmask\
    PainConstraints: Array<Constraint>\
    UserSelectionBias: SelectionBias Enum\
\
Output:\
    ResolvedSessionPlan: Array<ExerciseAssignment>\
\
Begin:\
    1. Set MaxSlots, MaxSets, MaxSetsPerSlot = LookupDurationRules(TimeBudgetMinutes)\
    2. CandidatePatterns = ResolvePatternSlotsForSplit(TargetMuscles)\
    \
    3. Filter CandidatePatterns:\
         For each pattern in CandidatePatterns:\
             If PainConstraints.Excludes(pattern):\
                 Remove pattern from CandidatePatterns\
                 \
    4. Compute DailyMuscleTargets:\
         For each muscle in TargetMuscles:\
             DailyMuscleTargets[muscle] = Ceiling(WeeklySetBudgets[muscle] / RemainingSessionsInMicrocycle[muscle])\
             \
    5. Initialize SessionPlan = Empty Array\
    6. Set RemainingSessionSets = MaxSets\
    \
    7. Sort CandidatePatterns by Priority (Primary Compounds -> Secondary Compounds -> Isolation)\
    \
    8. For each slot in CandidatePatterns:\
         If RemainingSessionSets <= 0 OR SessionPlan.Length >= MaxSlots:\
             Break Loop\
             \
         Set TargetMuscle = slot.PrimaryMuscle\
         If DailyMuscleTargets[TargetMuscle] <= 0:\
             Continue Loop\
             \
         Set EligibleExercises = QueryDatabase(slot.Pattern, EquipmentMask, PainConstraints)\
         If EligibleExercises is Empty:\
             Continue Loop\
             \
         Set SelectedExercise = RankAndSelect(EligibleExercises, UserSelectionBias)\
         \
         // Calculate set assignment\
         Set AllocatedSets = Minimum(DailyMuscleTargets[TargetMuscle], MaxSetsPerSlot)\
         Set AllocatedSets = Minimum(AllocatedSets, RemainingSessionSets)\
         \
         If AllocatedSets > 0:\
             Append ExerciseAssignment(SelectedExercise, AllocatedSets, slot.Pattern) to SessionPlan\
             \
             // Deduct Direct Volume Target\
             DailyMuscleTargets[TargetMuscle] -= AllocatedSets\
             RemainingSessionSets -= AllocatedSets\
             \
             // Apply Synergy Credits\
             For each synergist in SelectedExercise.SynergistList:\
                 If DailyMuscleTargets.Contains(synergist.Muscle):\
                     DailyMuscleTargets[synergist.Muscle] -= (AllocatedSets * 0.5)\
\
    9. Return SessionPlan\
End\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa160\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf2 \cb1 \strokec2 4. Volume & Experience Model\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa160\partightenfactor0

\fs28 \cf2 Critique of Static Experience Multipliers\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf2 Helm\'92s legacy volume seeding model applied fixed scalars ($0.85\\times$ Novice, $1.0\\times$ Intermediate, $1.1\\times$ Advanced) to static baseline landmarks. This approach presents significant physiological limitations. Training experience does not scale hypertrophic volume landmarks linearly. Novice lifters generate low fatigue per set and achieve robust muscle growth from low absolute set counts ($6$\'96$10$ sets/muscle/week), but possess limited work capacity. Conversely, highly advanced lifters recruit motor units more efficiently and produce far greater mechanical force per set, generating substantial localized micro-trauma and neurological fatigue. Consequently, an advanced athlete may hit their Maximum Recoverable Volume (MRV) at a lower set count for heavy compound lifts than an intermediate lifter.\
Helm replaces fixed experience scalars with an 
\f0\b Individualized Historical Baseline ($V_\{base\}$)
\f1\b0  model. Initial microcycle set targets are computed from the user's self-reported weekly hard sets over the preceding eight weeks, clamped within evidence-based starting boundaries:\
$$V_\{start\} = \\text\{Clamp\}\\left(V_\{reported\\_historical\\_average\}, \\, 8, \\, 15\\right)$$\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\fs28 \cf7 \cb8 \strokec7 USER ONBOARDING INPUT: Reported Average Hard Sets (Past 8 Weeks)\
  |\
  v\
ENGINE CLAMPING FUNCTION: Clamp(V_reported, Min: 8, Max: 15)\
  |\
  +---> Input: 5 sets/wk   --> Clamped Output: 8 sets/wk (MEV Baseline)\
  +---> Input: 12 sets/wk  --> Clamped Output: 12 sets/wk (Personalized Baseline)\
  +---> Input: 22 sets/wk  --> Clamped Output: 15 sets/wk (Safe Upper Ceiling)\
  |\
  v\
INITIAL MICROCYCLE SEED (V_start) -> Passed to PlanKit Engine\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa160\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf2 \cb1 \strokec2 Mid-Program Experience Multiplier Change Policy\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf2 If a user modifies their self-selected experience level mid-mesocycle, 
\fs30 \cf3 \cb4 \strokec3 PlanKit
\fs24 \cf2 \cb1 \strokec2  
\f0\b must not
\f1\b0  re-seed active microcycle set volumes. Modifying landmarks mid-block disrupts progressive overload progression and invalidates dynamic autoregulation data. Changes to experience settings are locked and only applied during the compilation of the 
\f0\b subsequent mesocycle block
\f1\b0 .\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa160\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs28 \cf2 Algorithmic Landmark Refinement Matrix\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf2 At the conclusion of each microcycle, 
\fs30 \cf3 \cb4 \strokec3 PlanKit
\fs24 \cf2 \cb1 \strokec2  refines individual muscle group MEV and MRV parameters using an empirical evaluation matrix combining logged Soreness (1\'964), Performance Progression (1\'964), and Average Weekly Readiness (ARC).\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\fs28 \cf7 \cb8 \strokec7 Soreness Metrics (S):\
  1: No soreness / fully recovered > 48h prior to next exposure\
  2: Recovered just in time for next session\
  3: Residual soreness present during subsequent session\
  4: Severe soreness impairing movement performance\
\
Performance Progression (P):\
  1: Exceeded load/rep targets with reserve (+2 RIR margin)\
  2: Met load/rep targets at prescribed RIR exactly\
  3: Failed target reps by 1-2 reps or missed target RIR\
  4: Performance regression (failed targets by > 2 reps across sets)\

