\f0\b\fs28 \cf2 Readiness Gating vs. MEV Floor Protection\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf2 Autoregulation must not depress training volume so frequently that an athlete spends consecutive weeks training below MEV.\
$$\\text\{Floor Constraint: If \} \\sum_\{i=1\}^\{2\} V_\{\\text\{actual\}, i\} < 2 \\times MEV \\quad \\Longrightarrow \\quad \\text\{Trigger Mandatory Plan Realignment\}$$\
If readiness gating depresses total weekly volume below MEV for two consecutive microcycles, the engine locks session set allocations at exact MEV baseline targets and enforces an increased proximity-to-failure buffer ($\\ge 3$ RIR). This preserves hypertrophy-stimulating volume while preventing excessive central fatigue accumulation.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\fs28 \cf7 \cb8 \strokec7 MICROCYCLE EVALUATION: Evaluate Logged Volume vs. MEV Baseline\
  |\
  +---> Has V_actual fallen below MEV for 2 consecutive weeks?\
  |         |\
  |         +---> YES: Trigger MEV Floor Protection\
  |         |           - Lock volume at exact MEV baseline\
  |         |           - Force Target RIR >= 3\
  |         |           - Suspend dynamic readiness set reductions\
  |         |\
  |         +---> NO:  Continue Standard Autoregulation Pipeline\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa160\partightenfactor0

