\fs24 \cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	1	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Non-Diagnostic Imperative
\f1\b0 : Helm does not provide medical diagnoses. The user interface strictly avoids clinical labels such as 
\f2\i "Patellofemoral Pain Syndrome"
\f1\i0  or 
\f2\i "Rotator Cuff Tendinitis."
\f1\i0  Pain inputs are categorized strictly as functional movement constraints (e.g., 
\fs30 \cf3 \cb4 \strokec3 Knee_Flexion_Pain_Gated
\fs24 \cf2 \cb1 \strokec2 ).\
\ls8\ilvl0
\f0\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	2	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Automated Care Referrals
\f1\b0 : If a user logs a Pain Severity Rating $\\ge 7/10$ during session tracking, or if joint pain persists for $>3$ consecutive weeks despite pattern substitutions, the engine locks progression for the affected muscle groups and displays a prompt advising evaluation by a licensed physical therapist or sports physician.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa160\partightenfactor0

