\f1\b0\fs24 \cf2 When a user enters free-text intent (e.g., 
\f2\i "I want to prioritize my arms and side delts"
\f1\i0 ), the LLM Coach converts the input into a structured engine payload rather than applying unstructured modifications:\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls10\ilvl0\cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	1	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 The LLM Coach parses the request and generates a 
\fs30 \cf3 \cb4 \strokec3 ProposalPayload
\fs24 \cf2 \cb1 \strokec2  JSON object specifying target muscle priorities.\
\ls10\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	2	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 The payload is sent to 
\fs30 \cf3 \cb4 \strokec3 PlanKit
\fs24 \cf2 \cb1 \strokec2  for validation against safety rules.\
\ls10\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	3	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 If validated, 
\fs30 \cf3 \cb4 \strokec3 PlanKit
\fs24 \cf2 \cb1 \strokec2  reallocates volume targets (e.g., increasing arm volume to $MAV$ while shifting non-emphasized muscles toward $MEV$).\
\ls10\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	4	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 The user receives a UI confirmation prompt outlining the proposed program adjustments before changes are committed to the training plan.\
