\fs28 \cf2 Nutrition Interface & Training Periodization\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf2 Nutritional state directly impacts muscular recovery capacity, altering training engine parameters across distinct dietary phases:\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls11\ilvl0
\f0\b \cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Caloric Deficit (Fat Loss / Cut Phase)
\f1\b0 : Systemic recovery capacity and muscle protein synthesis rates are attenuated. 
\fs30 \cf3 \cb4 \strokec3 PlanKit
\fs24 \cf2 \cb1 \strokec2  lowers default MRV caps by $15$\'96$25\\%$, halts progressive volume ramps once $MAV$ baseline is reached, and prioritizes absolute intensity of effort ($\\le 2$ RIR) over high volume accumulation to preserve lean mass.\
\ls11\ilvl0
\f0\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Caloric Surplus (Hypertrophy / Gain Phase)
\f1\b0 : Glycogen availability and systemic recovery capacities are optimized. 
\fs30 \cf3 \cb4 \strokec3 PlanKit
\fs24 \cf2 \cb1 \strokec2  enables aggressive volume progression rates ($+2\\text\{ to \}+3\\text\{ sets/week\}$) up to the full $MRV_\{hard\}$ ceiling.\
\ls11\ilvl0
\f0\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Low Energy Availability (LEA) & REDs Risk Signals
\f1\b0 : If an athlete logs persistent performance declines across $>2$ microcycles alongside low ARC readiness, elevated muscle soreness ($4/4$), and suppressed resting heart rate metrics, the engine flags potential LEA risk. The system restricts session volume to $MV$, locks RIR at $\\ge 3$, and prompts the user to evaluate their nutritional intake.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa160\partightenfactor0

